over the past generation tremendous  productivity growth has allowed the u.s.  dairy farms and processors to become  globally competitive however despite  this growth outdated policies that are  counterproductive to the dairy economy  remain in place such policies include  the 80 year-old Orwellian federal Milk  Marketing orders a concoction of  convoluted US pricing regulations the  selectively protectionist import  barriers that suited the old inefficient  US milk industry and lastly the recent  subsidized margin insurance scheme which  offers periodic payments designed to be  highly favorable to small inefficient  farms this program may become costly  harms lower-cost farms and adds little  to risk management these programs may  benefit some farms and processors often  the least productive but do so at the  expense of taxpayers consumers in the  broad dairy industry it is now time to  let the US milk producers and processors  embrace their global competitiveness and  innovate unencumbered by obsolete policy  approaches what do you think about US  dairy subsidy schemes let us know in  your comments also let us know what  other topics you'd like our scholars to  cover in 60 seconds and be sure to LIKE  and subscribe for more research and  videos from AEI
 

